snippet.description:
Patrick Bet-David discusses the often-overlooked risk of a power outage and its potential consequences, including disruptions to daily life, food spoilage, communication failures, and broader societal impacts. He highlights warnings from the Office of the Director of National Intelligence and Energy Secretary Jennifer Granholm regarding the capabilities of Russia, China, Iran, and North Korea to compromise the energy grid.

